      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1000 mg per dose. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **850 mg twice daily with meals** (1,700 mg/day)\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg** at a different frequency\n\nTell me the intended dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away. If 1700 mg three times daily is what you want, please confirm that and give me a reason for the note. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
